# Copy this to the product root as  .gitignore
#
# The entries in the FIRST block are generated by the toolkit on every run.
# If they are tracked, the deploy guard deadlocks permanently: running the gate
# creates the stamp file -> "you have uncommitted changes" -> commit it -> the
# commit changes the version -> "the checks passed on a different version" ->
# run the gate again -> stamp changes -> uncommitted again. Forever.

# --- generated by the toolkit, never edit or commit these --------------------
.oggi-gate-status.json
proof-cards.html
content-import.sql
content-replace.md
docs/.inventory-baseline.json
evidence/
_backups/

# NOTE: docs/FEATURE-LEDGER.generated.md and docs/feature-inventory.json ARE
# committed on purpose. The whole point is that they are diffed — that is how
# "this change removed something" becomes visible. Do not add them here.

# --- adoption baseline: COMMIT this, it is a shared record -------------------
# .oggi-adopted.json

# --- normal ------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
dist/
build/
.next/
coverage/
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- never commit a secret ---------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# --- toolkit installer leftovers: never commit these ------------------------
# These are artefacts of installing/updating the toolkit on a machine where
# files cannot be deleted through the file bridge. They are not part of the
# product and they made it into the first public commit, which is how this
# block came to exist.
_to_delete/
_update.tar.gz
*.tar.gz

# --- python bytecode --------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
